Reproduced. Fix in _get_meta_dict: convert non-string values to string. itk 5.3 returns native itk objects for non-string metadata. Best fix: convert value to str if not a str/int/float? Actually meta values previously were strings. Simplest: `str(img_meta_dict[key])`? But older itk already returns strings, str() no-op. But stringifying a matrix gives "itkMatrixF44 (...)" which loses data. Better: keep values that are str/number, otherwise convert to numpy array if possible, else str.

Fix:
```python
meta_dict = {
    key: img_meta_dict[key] for key in img_meta_dict.GetKeys() if not key.startswith("ITK_")
}
# convert to string if needed
for k, v in meta_dict.items():
    if not isinstance(v, (str, int, float, np.ndarray)):
        try:
            v = np.asarray(v)
        except Exception:
            v = str(v)
```
For itkMatrixF44, np.asarray may work? itk matrix supports __array__? Check.

